[{"text":"ExpandScalarProduct[expr] expands scalar products of sums of momenta in expr.","anchor":"expandscalarproduct"},{"text":"ExpandScalarProduct does not use Expand on expr.","anchor":"expandscalarproduct"},{"text":"Overview, Calc, MomentumExpand, MomentumCombine, FCVariable","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"SP[p1 + p2 + p3, p4 + p5 + p6] % // ExpandScalarProduct","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"(\\overline{\\text{p1}}+\\overline{\\text{p2}}+\\overline{\\text{p3}})\\cdot (\\overline{\\text{p4}}+\\overline{\\text{p5}}+\\overline{\\text{p6}})","anchor":"cb1-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{\\text{p1}}\\cdot \\overline{\\text{p4}}+\\overline{\\text{p1}}\\cdot \\overline{\\text{p5}}+\\overline{\\text{p1}}\\cdot \\overline{\\text{p6}}+\\overline{\\text{p2}}\\cdot \\overline{\\text{p4}}+\\overline{\\text{p2}}\\cdot \\overline{\\text{p5}}+\\overline{\\text{p2}}\\cdot \\overline{\\text{p6}}+\\overline{\\text{p3}}\\cdot \\overline{\\text{p4}}+\\overline{\\text{p3}}\\cdot \\overline{\\text{p5}}+\\overline{\\text{p3}}\\cdot \\overline{\\text{p6}}\\]","anchor":"cb1-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"SP[p, p - q] ExpandScalarProduct[%]","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}\\cdot (\\overline{p}-\\overline{q})\\]","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}^2-\\overline{p}\\cdot \\overline{q}\\]","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"FV[p - q, \\[Mu]] ExpandScalarProduct[%]","anchor":"cb3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\left(\\overline{p}-\\overline{q}\\right)^{\\mu }","anchor":"cb3-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{p}^{\\mu }-\\overline{q}^{\\mu }\\]","anchor":"cb3-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"SPD[p - q, q - r] ExpandScalarProduct[%]","anchor":"cb4","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[(p-q)\\cdot (q-r)\\]","anchor":"cb4-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[p\\cdot q-p\\cdot r+q\\cdot r-q^2\\]","anchor":"cb4-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Using the option Momentum one can limit the expansion to particular momenta","anchor":"cb4-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"SP[p1 + p2 + p3, p4 + p5 + p6] ExpandScalarProduct[%, Momentum -> {p1}]","anchor":"cb5","section":"Examples"},{"text":"(\\overline{\\text{p1}}+\\overline{\\text{p2}}+\\overline{\\text{p3}})\\cdot (\\overline{\\text{p4}}+\\overline{\\text{p5}}+\\overline{\\text{p6}})","anchor":"cb5-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\overline{\\text{p1}}\\cdot (\\overline{\\text{p4}}+\\overline{\\text{p5}}+\\overline{\\text{p6}})+(\\overline{\\text{p2}}+\\overline{\\text{p3}})\\cdot (\\overline{\\text{p4}}+\\overline{\\text{p5}}+\\overline{\\text{p6}})\\]","anchor":"cb5-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"By default ExpandScalarProduct does not apply linearity to Levi-Civita tensors","anchor":"cb5-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"LC[\\[Mu]][p1 + p2, p3 + p4, p5 + p6] ExpandScalarProduct[%]","anchor":"cb6","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\overline{\\text{p1}}+\\overline{\\text{p2}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p3}}+\\overline{\\text{p4}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p5}}+\\overline{\\text{p6}}}\\]","anchor":"cb6-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\overline{\\text{p1}}+\\overline{\\text{p2}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p3}}+\\overline{\\text{p4}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p5}}+\\overline{\\text{p6}}}\\]","anchor":"cb6-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Using the option EpsEvaluate takes care of that","anchor":"cb6-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"LC[\\[Mu]][p1 + p2, p3 + p4, p5 + p6] ExpandScalarProduct[%, EpsEvaluate -> True]","anchor":"cb7","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\overline{\\text{p1}}+\\overline{\\text{p2}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p3}}+\\overline{\\text{p4}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p5}}+\\overline{\\text{p6}}}\\]","anchor":"cb7-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\overline{\\text{p1}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p3}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p5}}}+\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\overline{\\text{p1}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p3}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p6}}}+\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\overline{\\text{p1}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p4}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p5}}}+\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\overline{\\text{p1}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p4}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p6}}}+\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\overline{\\text{p2}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p3}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p5}}}+\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\overline{\\text{p2}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p3}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p6}}}+\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\overline{\\text{p2}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p4}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p5}}}+\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\overline{\\text{p2}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p4}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p6}}}\\]","anchor":"cb7-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"One can use the options EpsEvaluate and Momentum together","anchor":"cb7-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"LC[\\[Mu]][p1 + p2, p3 + p4, p5 + p6] ExpandScalarProduct[%, EpsEvaluate -> True, Momentum -> {p1}]","anchor":"cb8","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\overline{\\text{p1}}+\\overline{\\text{p2}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p3}}+\\overline{\\text{p4}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p5}}+\\overline{\\text{p6}}}\\]","anchor":"cb8-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\overline{\\text{p1}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p3}}+\\overline{\\text{p4}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p5}}+\\overline{\\text{p6}}}+\\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\overline{\\text{p2}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p3}}+\\overline{\\text{p4}}\\;\\overline{\\text{p5}}+\\overline{\\text{p6}}}\\]","anchor":"cb8-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Of course, the function is also applicable to Cartesian quantities","anchor":"cb8-3","section":"Examples"}]